{"author":{"id":"f21006d1826991d76b358f177209294474e8c2701fc659ff8fe8b8f40ee77f55"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1677775106,"nonce":"59Tq8O3/KJEyUFvlNQTRr2YDDPA=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh85Wjmxi","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/327#issuecomment-1452174434"},"message":"If we're looking for a cross-platform solution, letting the user pick how their credentials are stored and using `git-credential` is actually what I'd argue for, since that is a) available in Git, requiring no additional user-managed dependency, and b) not limiting the user to supported secret backends (e.g. a particular keyring).\n\nI do not have `gnome-keyring` installed, and have no desire to install it just so I can use it for managing my `git-bug` credentials -- I'd much prefer to use my existing password store.","files":null}]}